{"title":"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A palindrome is a positive integer whose digits are the same when read forwards or backwards. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8ecff4d54fd1d24f2f281fc89348934c8629bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25352$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> is a five-digit palindrome. What is the largest five-digit palindrome that is a multiple of 15? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the number is a five digit palindrome, we see that the format of the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82dae56b405b0ca36af28d3491e8840cae4b054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XYZYX}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are digits.\n</p><p>If the number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we realize that the number must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dda8115d8d4a649a1736b3797df21af5fbb54fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 3 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>First, if the number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096cf8cb0ad774f7cae6d6eafdedb9db737fbcf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3fbbc632f18d767ad1d9e7af1fa841452c13a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. However, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is also the ten-thousands digit, it cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3fbbc632f18d767ad1d9e7af1fa841452c13a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. This means that the number must be in the format <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8ecef4deb8f2bd0c744942c3b6d99f3a05bb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{5YZY5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Next, if the number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the sum of the digits must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of the digits is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b02440c4bd1100075dc06d3f3d831fa146e3a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 2 + 2Y + Z = 10 + 2Y + Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"248\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>For the number to be the largest one, we want to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, so we can set it to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f54c30bbb9d536a68c20baa4a149fe80d8236b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 2 \\times 9 + Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the remainder can further be reduced to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d61c67d97aa4e492b1cf87ec3341a02901be8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>For this to have a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> must then have a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is maximized by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313c4b7c086f78494ed7afafd12ff89bac71a6ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Combining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3fbbc632f18d767ad1d9e7af1fa841452c13a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404fecd9c732bc2c7596f61b1a84630170322656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313c4b7c086f78494ed7afafd12ff89bac71a6ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ead384f462ced4705a48327579a287961bb9ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{59895}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"59\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC\">2016 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" 